<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Farrukhi Sistani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1038</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Farrukhi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Farrukhi Sistani was a Persian poet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a> who served at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> and his son Mas'ud I. He is known for his panegyric odes celebrating the Ghaznavid sultans and their campaigns, including the expedition to Somnath, written in a clear and graceful style, and is counted among the leading poets of early classical Persian literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/farrukhi-sistani.jpg" alt="Farrukhi Sistani" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Darvîsh 'Abdî (calligrapher) · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Firdaus%C3%AE_approaches_the_three_poets_of_Sh%C3%A2h_Mahm%C3%BBd_who_sit_reading_while_servants_prepare_meat_on_a_spit_behind_them.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
